    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 97116,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97116.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "All right. So, Mr. Chairman, you, of course, led this very important committee in Congress. And I want to go through some of the highlights of your time as chairman, starting with the American Rescue Plan, this landmark piece of legislation that Basically, save the American economy to build it. You spent a lot of time on it. I want to focus on one part of that, which is pensions. A lot of people, their retirement security was at risk because when the economy was in danger there, you had a lot of people that might not have gotten the pensions that they worked for for many, many years. So you put together a special financial assistance program. Some of our listeners might be familiar with SFA program. Tell us a little bit about this SFA program and how that saved people's pensions. I saw your committee has a running tally here. And I think currently this legislation has already saved like 200,000 pensions and 1,000 businesses have been protected. How does this system work?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker will take a moment to thank their colleagues on the committee.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The colleagues on the committee assisted in crafting the policy.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The colleagues on the committee contributed to delivering results.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Collaboration with colleagues is essential for effective policymaking.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Public recognition of team effort strengthens political legitimacy and unity.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Colleagues' contributions were significant enough to warrant acknowledgment.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Expressing gratitude reinforces trust and cohesion within the legislative group.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 97116,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97116.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, what we're talking about is a multi-employer pension fund. There are a lot of workers that work for very short periods of time with an employer in construction, for example, when the project is finished, they go on and do another job, probably another employer. And under the multi-employer pension fund, the participating employers will pay into the pension fund, pay into the account of the various employees. And then when the retirement comes, the employee will have one full retirement account. The problem occurred with bankruptcies and the 08 financial crisis and lacks oversight by the federal government. A lot of these plans were in trouble. We calculated, if we didn't do anything, about a million people would lose their pensions. And also because all of the employers involved and jointly and simply obligated to pay into the plans until the business one broke, a lot of businesses, tens of thousands of businesses were at financial risk. We calculated that if we didn't do anything, the people who lose their pensions would pay less income tax, so it would be more likely to use SNAP benefits and Medicaid. to the tune of about $170 billion in the next 10 years, and a lot more after that. We were able to come up with a solution for about half that cost. So we saved money, we saved a million people's pensions, and we saved tens of thousands of businesses by taking proactive initiatives in the American Rescue Plan. And we were able to provide financial security during retirement for about a million people and saved about tens of thousands of businesses at risk of collapsing because of their obligation to these funds.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "A multi-employer pension fund involves multiple employers contributing to a single retirement account for employees.",
        "confidence": 0.98
      },
      {
        "text": "Workers in industries like construction often have short-term employment relationships with individual employers.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Under the multi-employer pension system, employers are jointly and severally liable for funding the plan.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The 2008 financial crisis and lack of federal oversight caused many multi-employer pension plans to become financially unstable.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Without intervention, approximately one million people would lose their pension benefits.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Without intervention, tens of thousands of businesses would face significant financial risk due to pension obligations.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "If pension beneficiaries lost their pensions, they would likely rely more on public assistance programs such as SNAP and Medicaid.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The projected increase in public assistance usage due to pension losses would amount to roughly $170 billion over ten years.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "A solution was implemented through the American Rescue Plan that reduced costs by about half compared to doing nothing.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The proactive policy initiative preserved approximately one million retirement accounts and protected tens of thousands of businesses from collapse.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
