        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Businesses' ability to survive depends significantly on predictable and manageable liability structures.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Economic outcomes can be meaningfully quantified using cost-benefit frameworks involving future public spending.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Proactive legislative action is more effective than reactive crisis management in complex financial systems.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Pension benefits represent a legitimate expectation of worker compensation and deserve protection.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Federal oversight is necessary to prevent widespread failures in decentralized but interdependent pension systems.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "The success of the American Rescue Plan in addressing this issue demonstrates its broader effectiveness in economic recovery.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "Individuals who lose pensions are more likely to experience long-term poverty and dependency on state support.",
